WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:04.009
If you want to hear how one dark detail from
the book was hidden in this mini-series then

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:05.900
stick around to this end of this video.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.580
This video is brought to you by Raid: Shadow
Legends.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.780
If you’ve seen some of my other It videos,
you know that one of my favorite side-characters

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:19.159
from the book is the foul mouthed cab driver.

00:00:19.159 --> 00:00:22.050
And while we don’t get to listen to his
banter in the mini-series, part 2 does open

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:26.839
up with Bill being dropped off in a cab at the
cemetery where he has his first Pennywise

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:27.940
encounter since returning to Derry.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:37.220
“Take your pick, B-b-b-billy boy!

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.120
Oh!

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.300
Except for the one on the end.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.740
That’s already taken.”

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.300
This seems to be a reference to Stan being
the one out of the lucky 7 who already died,

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.649
although, it would have been more accurate
if Pennywise had given him a Jewish grave

00:00:51.649 --> 00:00:52.649
marker.

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:55.970
After this encounter, Bill visits Mike at
the library, where there is a table set up

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.640
dedicated to his works as an author.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.820
The title Gnaw could be a reference to the
unnamed werewolf novel Stan’s wife was reading

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.940
in the book, and The Glowing could either
be a reference to the glowing Deadlights or

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.720
a parody of one of Stephen King’s well known
books: The Shining.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.900
Meanwhile, Richie Tozier is rolling into town
singing The Beach Boys

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.760
"...this same old strip
I got to find a new place where the kids are hip."

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.740
When he notices his

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.920
own epitaph on the movie theater marquee.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:21.790
This is a reimagining of a scene in the book
where he finds a similar inscription on a

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.110
rock concert poster in the park.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:27.090
He runs into the library to find Mike, but
instead, finds Pennywise, who is reading the

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.490
finance section of the newspaper?

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:32.350
Is this supposed to be a joke about It’s
name being Pennywise?

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.350
Really guys?

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:37.670
Back at Mike’s house, the boys are rediscovering
Bill’s old bike, Silver, and Mike brings

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.240
out the playing cards.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.400
“Not just any cards.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.400
Bicycle."

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.600
"They always made the best noise."

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.610
Bill and Mike notice something is wrong when
they see two Ace of Spades, and the Pennywise

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:53.890
design on the back of the cards, very similar
to the book, where they open a brand new deck,

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:56.630
but there are blue and red back cards mixed
in with each other.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:00.420
It is at about this time that Ben arrives
in Derry, and goes down into the Barrens where

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.700
he sees a fat boy getting bullied, giving
him flashbacks to his childhood.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.090
He helps fix up the boy’s scraped knee…

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.640
Ohh ohhhh no.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.890
That cannot be sanitary.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:12.190
“It’s basically piss and **** that all
I’m just telling you.”

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.040
Eddie is the next to arrive back in town.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.890
He visits the pharmacy, where he picks up
his asthma medication and runs into Mr. Keene,

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:19.840
the pharmacist from when he was young.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.420
“Hydrox."

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:23.100
"What?"

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.540
H20.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.500
Water!"

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.150
But this is only another example of Pennywise
manipulating the town of Derry.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.480
Mr. Keene grabs onto Eddie using a hand covered
in a crunchy exoskeleton like that of the

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.640
spider claw that the seven of them drove away
Pennywise as kids.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.840
The last to arrive is Beverly Marsh who visits
her father’s old home.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:46.540
There are three names next to the doorbells
of this townhouse: Marsh, Burke and Starkeweather.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.000
Burke and Starkeweather are the family names
of the second and third floor occupants of

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.360
Beverly’s apartment in the book.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.890
This house doesn’t appear to have a third
floor, but maybe Starkweather is around back

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:58.510
here, I’ve still got to applaud the accuracy
of that small detail from the novel.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:02.980
When Beverly gets away, Mrs. Kersh transforms
into the clown off screen…

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.000
...and we hear that same noise heard when
Richie’s werewolf turns into Pennywise…

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.940
…which is also heard by Stan, later on in
the sewers.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:21.680
The remaining members of the Lucky 7 would
reconvene for a reunion dinner, where even

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.620
more hidden details can be uncovered.

