00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.240
Remember Bill’s wife Audra, the actress?

00:04:17.249 --> 00:04:21.469
She’s extremely concerned about her husband
after his sudden trek back to Derry, and she

00:04:21.469 --> 00:04:25.040
meets with the movie producer about his sudden
disappearance from set.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.680
“You’ve worked very hard to get where
you are, very hard.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.290
I know you’d do nothing to jeopardize that.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.820
Or to damage our professional relationship.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:40.320
Or to turn a friend overnight into a violent
enemy, ready to crucify you at at cost.”

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.820
WHOA.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.420
That escalated, so fast.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.400
Wake up!

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.819
Grab a brush and put a little makeup!

00:04:45.819 --> 00:04:49.069
Richie has a momentary panic attack after
realizing his old friends are all grown up

00:04:49.069 --> 00:04:51.080
now and stops in the bathroom to get ahold
of himself.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:54.860
I recently noticed that he knocks over the
artwork in the bathroom and never fixes it.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.930
After the introductions, they discuss Pennywise.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:58.460
“Maybe that means he’s afraid.”

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:58.960
“It.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.140
It’s afraid.”

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.050
This little correction is a reference to a
more significant detail in the book, being

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.659
that the creature It is actually a female,
something that Audra discovers upon being

00:05:07.659 --> 00:05:09.169
taken to the spider’s lair.

00:05:09.169 --> 00:05:14.990
“The writer’s woman had put out one powerful,
horrified thought—OH DEAR JESUS IT IS FEMALE—and

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:16.740
then all thoughts ceased.”

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:20.360
Eddie is the only one whose memory about what
happened to them as children has yet to come

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:23.980
back, and after hearing the word ‘sewer’,
the cloud over his memories dissipates in

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:24.560
a rush.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:27.880
“I think I remember who Pennywise was now.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.780
Big white guy.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.050
Red nose.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.120
About 75 feet tall?”

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.310
75 feet tall?

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.310
No.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.389
No what are you talking about Eddie?

00:05:36.389 --> 00:05:38.080
He was never 75 feet tall.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:41.819
The six of them decide to save the serious
topic of conversation for later and enjoy

00:05:41.819 --> 00:05:45.339
their meal, and the music during the food
montage is the same song from the building

00:05:45.339 --> 00:05:49.120
of the dam 30 years ago, because they are
rebuilding those bonds they had formed together

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.220
as children.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:53.710
After chowing down, they get to discussing
the reason they all came back to Derry: the

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.520
promise that they would eradicate Pennywise
once more.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:00.150
The camera circles around them in this scene
giving the viewer a sense of disorientation

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:03.930
as they recall more and more disturbing things
from their past; their heads are spinning

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:07.210
trying to process it all, and the cinematography
reflects that.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:10.779
Finally, their fortune cookies arrive, and
each cookie contains something that represents

00:06:10.779 --> 00:06:11.789
one of their fears.

00:06:11.789 --> 00:06:14.300
Beverly’s is the blood, like the blood from
her father’s sink.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:18.159
Eddie’s is a roach, a bug associated with
poor sanitation and somewhat similar to his

00:06:18.159 --> 00:06:20.719
adult fear from the book: the crickets in
his basement.

00:06:20.719 --> 00:06:24.279
Richie’s is an eyeball, because he was always
bullied for his glasses as kid.

00:06:24.279 --> 00:06:27.480
Mike’s is a bird hatchling, referencing
his fear of the giant bird that attacked him

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.480
in the book.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.749
I honestly have no idea what Ben’s is, but
Bill’s seems to be a spider, yet another

00:06:31.749 --> 00:06:36.610
clue about the eventual final form of It that
these six would come to face.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.460
After fleeing the restaurant, they continue
their meeting at the library, where they try

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.999
to get ahold of Stan and learn about his death.

00:06:41.999 --> 00:06:45.530
Bill recalls Stan’s childhood encounter
with It as further evidence of how Stan was

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:47.439
so deeply affected by the monster.

00:06:47.439 --> 00:06:49.539
In the flashback, Stan wanders into an old
house.

00:06:49.539 --> 00:06:53.689
Not only is this scene a substitute for Stan’s
horrifying journey into The Standpipe in the

00:06:53.689 --> 00:06:57.930
book, where he gets trapped inside the water
storage structure in a similar way and has

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.380
to use his bird book to free himself; but
I think the house itself is supposed to be

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:05.770
29 Neibolt Street, an abandoned old property
that serves as It’s bridge between the sewers

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:06.930
and the surface.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:10.720
We don’t fully see the figure that left
a permanent scar on Stan’s memories, but

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:13.659
from what we do see, it appears to be a Mummy
in the clown suit.

00:07:13.659 --> 00:07:17.430
This was likely supposed to be the same mummy
that Ben encounters in the novel on the canal

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:21.509
bridge, and finds to be much more disturbing
than Boris Karloff’s depiction of The Mummy

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:23.599
in the 1932 film.

00:07:23.599 --> 00:07:27.030
Pennywise tries to scare them off my hitting
the library with an indoor thunderstorm, so

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:31.310
they gather up the supplies Mike has organized
and head to the hotel that Bill, Eddie, Richie,

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.999
Beverly and Ben are staying at.

00:07:32.999 --> 00:07:37.020
The stuff Mike collected consists of boxes
of hardhats, pairs of boots and flashlights.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.410
The hardhats never actually get used though.

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:43.659
Throughout the night, Pennywise contacts Henry
Bowers, who is locked up in Juniper Hill Insane

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:45.900
Asylum, as a figure that appears to him through
the moon.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.960
The guard at the asylum is named Koontz, named
after Stephen King’s rival Dean Koontz,

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.520
a fellow horror author.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:54.210
When It appears before Koontz, he drops a
roll of quarters.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:58.409
The mini-series never explains why, but in
the novel, quarters are used as a form of

00:07:58.409 --> 00:08:00.449
punishment on the patients fo the asylum.

00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:04.159
“It was illegal for the guards (who were
called “counsellors” here at Juniper Hill)

00:08:04.159 --> 00:08:08.990
to carry billyclubs, so a number of them—Fogarty,
Adler, and Koontz were the worst—carried

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:10.580
rolls of quarters in their pockets.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:13.689
They almost always hit you with them in the
same place, right in the back of the neck.

00:08:13.689 --> 00:08:15.860
There was no rule against quarters.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:18.360
Quarters were not considered a deadly weapon
at Juniper Hill.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:22.580
Back at the Inn, Mike hands out copies of
his collection of newspaper headlines corresponding

00:08:22.589 --> 00:08:24.599
to tragic events in Derry’s past.

00:08:24.599 --> 00:08:28.199
The first headline reads ‘Blackspot Club
Burns’, a story about the nightclub that

00:08:28.199 --> 00:08:30.409
Mike’s father narrowly escaped in the novel.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:32.930
On the back there’s a piece on Derry’s
Lost Settlers.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:36.699
The book tells of an Irish group of settlers
named the Derry Company that disappeared without

00:08:36.699 --> 00:08:39.229
leaving a trace before the town as we know
it was established.

00:08:39.229 --> 00:08:43.419
There are a couple of mistakes on this paper,
for example the date listed is April 26, 1960,

00:08:43.419 --> 00:08:45.660
which was a Tuesday, not a Wednesday.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:49.240
The content of the articles doesn’t correspond
to what is teased in the headlines either.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:52.069
In fact, the clickbait is so strong here that
you’d think these articles were written

00:08:52.069 --> 00:08:53.440
by Lance Stewart.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:56.810
This one is about The Arctic and this one
is about politics or something.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:09:00.279
As they all leave the hotel for the last time,
the woman at the desk has a few copies of

00:09:00.279 --> 00:09:04.480
Bill's book, The Glowing, and what looks to
a vinyl with Richie's name and gave on it.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.880
She's got a pen ready, as if she's about to
ask for autographs, but they all leave so

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.970
quickly she doesn't have the chance.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:14.000
Before stepping out, Bill sees a woman and
child playing Fur Elise by Beethoven.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.920
This is the same song his mother always used
to play.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:28.960
What remains of the group packs into Richie's
car to drive to down to the sewer and take

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:29.970
down Pennywise.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:34.529
The model of this car is an IROC-Z, perhaps
chosen to signify Richie's love for Rock and

00:09:34.529 --> 00:09:35.529
Roll.

00:09:35.529 --> 00:09:38.620
When they get down into the sewer pipes, spider
webs cover the walls, a grim clue about the

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:40.910
creature they would face later that night.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:44.490
The first form of It they encounter is Bill's
deceased little brother Georgie.

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:48.790
Although we never see Georgie's death on screen,
the child is missing his right arm, a reminder

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:52.870
for fans of the book of the disturbing method
of his death, where his arm is dismembered.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:56.810
In the cavern, we finally discover the meaning
of It's catch phrase, "you'll float too".

00:09:56.810 --> 00:10:00.940
The bodies of the victims float over the chamber,
strung up in the spider's webbing.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:04.860
Also there's the fact that this is clearly
a painting, but who's to say It came have

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.080
a taste for the fine arts?

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.769
It is at this point that I would have liked
for everyone to realize that Bill's wife is

00:10:09.769 --> 00:10:14.320
the movie star, Audra Phillips, and yell out,
"Hey, It got the lady from Black Christmas!"

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.540
Yeah that doesn't happen though...

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:19.320
The original plan for this final boss battle
was to have Tim Curry, the man who played

00:10:19.339 --> 00:10:23.750
Pennywise in control of the spider somehow,
but that didn't pan out, so instead the only

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:27.899
resemblance is when the creature briefly flashes
its carnivorous teeth, just like the clown

00:10:27.899 --> 00:10:29.510
is sometimes seem to have.

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:30.750
Then this happens.

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:33.980
“I believe in Santa Claus.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.180
I believe in the Easter Bunny.

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:39.700
I believe in the tooth fairy.”

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.940
“Eddie, Eddie, what are you saying, you're a virgin?”

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:42.880
And they beat It.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:44.740
They kill the monster.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:48.490
I love this mini series, but that isn't my
favorite part.

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:52.690
As things wrap, we learn that Richie Tozier
got into movies after returning to Hollywood.

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:56.560
The movie that he's shown shooting is in on
Scene 574!?

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:58.640
Oh my, that is a long movie.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:00.519
And I thought It was long.

00:11:00.519 --> 00:11:02.670
There's also an easter egg on the slate.

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:07.870
The cinematographer of Richie's movie, J Bereziuk,
is the name of the script supervisor in IT.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.600
Bill is still rehabilitating his wife when
it's time to leave.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:14.550
The same cab driver from way back at the beginning
picks him up, but he wants to try one more

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:18.600
thing first to try to save Audra and takes
her for a spin on his old bike, Silver.

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:21.040
"This bike saved little Stan's life once.

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:22.800
Mine too.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.660
We were going so fast I think we beat the
devil.”

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:29.980
Like in It Chapter 2, this is an audible reference
to the epilogue's chapter title: Bill Denbrough

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:31.020
beats the devil.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:35.649
The film goes to black, and everyone gets
their happy ending… or do they?

00:11:35.649 --> 00:11:39.960
Over the credits, Pennywise's laughter can
be heard continuing to reverberate.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:45.640
"AHHH ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha..."

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:52.640
Could this imply that Pennywise lives on after
this second defeat at the hands of Bill, Bev,

00:11:52.649 --> 00:11:53.649
Ben and Richie?

00:11:53.649 --> 00:11:57.560
The idea of explored more in Stephen King's
other books, so make sure you watch my Horror

00:11:57.560 --> 00:11:59.959
History episode on Pennywise video to find
out.

00:11:59.959 --> 00:12:04.600
But before you move on, make sure you subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:08.449
that deathbell for notifications and I'll
see you in the next one.

00:12:08.449 --> 00:12:09.839
Assuming we both survive.

